KG42.register("rules-21975fd3997d1a784d560dea",{"id":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R003","paper":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R003","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Consumers are permitted to participate in P2P trade within the community. Scope: Local P2P trade within the community. Condition: P2P trade is enabled, as in the P2P and STEP market cases.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.consumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Local P2P trade within the community.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e38"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Consumers are permitted to participate in P2P trade within the community. Scope: Local P2P trade within the community. Condition: P2P trade is enabled, as in the P2P and STEP market cases.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e38"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e02","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"market. In this paper, the market design allows P2P trade among ec- prosumers and consumers in a com","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this paper, the market design allows P2P trade among prosumers and consumers in a community. Peers can trade locally produced and stored energy at a dynamic, half-hourly varying P2P price. Some prosumers and consumers have own batteries that can be charged with local generation and from the grid (see, e.g., [26])."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e38","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p09-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"As of today, electricity end-users are at the end of the supply era chain in a still predominant top","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Today’s UK market under dynamic pricing – assuming smart metering – serves in this paper as our base case. To identify the value of each of the proposed local market features – P2P trade and battery storage –, three further cases are compared to the base case: We add P2P trade and battery storage possibilities one by one to investigate their sole values to the system. In short, we apply our model to four cases that distinguish by their options of battery storage and P2P trade. The possibility of feeding from the community into the grid is enabled in all cases. We define the following: • The Base case is defined as today’s electricity market under dynamic real-time pricing. It is not possible to directly trade with other peers, and no electricity storage possibilities are deployed within this case. • The BAT market introduces the possibility of battery storage. Direct trade between the peers is disabled. • The P2P market includes the direct P2P trade connection in the community. The possibility of storage is, however, not implemented. • The STEP market offers both battery storage and P2P trade options within the community."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"This rule is a procedural consumer-admission permission. The source evidence identifies no design-selection or operational decision quantity that is optimized or chosen by consumers under this specific permission.","empty_theta_reason":"The source evidence gives no fixed numeric or symbolic parameter for consumer participation. The stated condition that P2P trade is enabled is a case-scope condition, not a quantified parameter value in this rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e02","quote":"In this paper, the market design allows P2P trade among prosumers and consumers in a community."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e38","quote":"The P2P market includes the direct P2P trade connection in the community."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e38","quote":"The STEP market offers both battery storage and P2P trade options within the community."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"cb7a3ec6516101faf9bde24de47de4ca4d56377cfa9745ab6a435a66d63d01fd","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The supplied source text states that the market design allows P2P trade among prosumers and consumers in a community, and the case definitions identify direct P2P trade as enabled in the P2P and STEP market cases. For consumers, this is a procedural permission to participate in local P2P trade, not a mathematical relation; no equation, quantitative eligibility test, or parameter value is stated for consumer participation in this rule. The phi entry therefore remains not_formalized with expression null.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The constraint is the unary consumer-participation permission attached to the frozen node participation.consumer. The supplied graph has no edges for this rule, and the source states a procedural permission rather than a mathematical relation."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
